"""The mutants of K11 (epoch readback). Each row: (name, target, exact anchor, replacement). The anchor must occur
exactly once in every file the target is applied to (mutate.py check). Target 'op' is the operation's own part as it
stands in build/epoch_readback.py; 'docker', 'lock' and 'core' are the carried parts in that same file, for the few
guarantees of the core this operation leans on in a way the core's own demonstrations do not.
One mutant per refusal of validate_plan, one per member of effects_of(), one per finding and per gate of perform, one
per check of the line the container prints, and the words of the pinned snippet."""
M=[]
def add(name,target,old,new):M.append((name,target,old,new))
def op(name,old,new):add(name,'op',old,new)

